he definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{m}=a+mΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{6}ln⁡(4x-3)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=ln⁡(4x-3),$ the lower bound is $a=1$ and the upper bound is $b=6.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{6-1}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}ln⁡(4x-3)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(1+m\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(1+\\frac{5m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(4(1+\\frac{5m}{n})-3)\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(1+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533624 true] [17592186242473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242474 13194139533624 true] [17592186242473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242475 13194139533624 true] [17592186242473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242476 13194139533624 true] [17592186242473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242477 13194139533624 true] [17592186242473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242478 13194139533624 true] [17592186242473 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533624 true] [17592186242473 1041 "selection" 13194139533624 true] [17592186242473 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242478 13194139533624 true] [17592186242473 1110 #uuid "d9577d8c-6531-5709-9143-3624f0d1ce8c" 13194139533624 true] [17592186242474 1034 "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[(1+\\frac{20m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]" 13194139533624 true] [17592186242474 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533624 true] [17592186242474 1111 #uuid "146ce130-ceaa-58c7-86da-de41f259154a" 13194139533624 true] [17592186242475 1034 "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[ln⁡(1+\\frac{5m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n